  Slug: sponsored-by-a-village
  DisplayName: Sponsored by a Village
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/background.svg
  Description: 'You come from a small community far from any large cities, but the
    Magaambya is known even in your isolated corner of the world. You have shown
    more scholarly talent than anyone from your village in many years, perhaps even
    generations, and the village elders have insisted you explore your potential
    at the Magaambya. Whether you were eager to leave or not seemed irrelevant to
    the elders; you had the talent, so you must go. You don''t know how the elders
    had the connections or influence to sponsor your education there, but you''ve
    left your tight- knit community behind for the city of Nantambu and the Magaambya
    at its heart. Choose two attribute boosts. One must be to Intelligence or Wisdom
    , and one is a free attribute boost. You''re trained in your choice of the Crafting
    or Survival skill. You gain a skill feat: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Crafter''s
    Appraisal] if you chose Crafting or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Forager]
    if you chose Survival. You''re also trained in the Lore skill appropriate for
    the terrain around your community (such as Forest Lore or Jungle Lore). Your
    recommended primary branch is the Cascade Bearers.'
  SourceTitle: Pathfinder Strength of Thousands Player's Guide
  SourcePack: backgrounds
  Rarity: uncommon
  SourceJsonHash: f730655561e640f3d23dc6bf8c2f09988e6368e7f65d4303c1ffea2329266900
